 "source_instruction": "i am looking for 2 pack of 20ft long quadshield solid copper black color indoor and outdoor coaxial cable",
 "query": "I spent all last weekend helping my neighbor fix up the old treehouse in his backyard for his two kids, and it was way more of a project than either of us expected. We had to replace three rotted floor planks, string up a whole new set of fairy lights that keep shorting out every time a breeze picks up, and even hauled up a little fold-down table so the kids can color and have snacks up there when the weather\u2019s nice. Yesterday he texted me a photo of them hanging out in it with their pet guinea pig, who was tucked into a tiny makeshift harness they\u2019d rigged out of old ribbon so he wouldn\u2019t tumble through the railing gaps, and it made all the splinters and sore back muscles totally worth it. I\u2019m browsing the satellite television section right now. I have a setup that uses triaxial cable. I\u2019ve heard the quadshield solid copper version in black works well for this, and that the multi-pack length option is a solid fit. I\u2019ve also heard none of the options that fit those parameters go over $40 total.",
